How We Built a Procedural 3D Massing Engine for CRE in 9 KB of JavaScript

When we set out to build the **Keystone Asset Management** template — a white-label institutional CRE landing page — the 3D massing study was the differentiator. Not a decorative hero. A functional underwriting tool.

The brief: investors need to *see* the asset. Floor plates, glazing ratios, clear heights, vertical zoning. And they need it before capital is committed.

The constraint: **no external model files**. No GLB, no CDN, no 50 MB download. The template had to be a single deployable artifact — `npm run build` → `dist/` → Vercel.

---

## The Architecture

```
dist/
├── index.html                    # 23 KB (with JSON-LD, CSP, modal)
├── assets/
│   ├── index-*.js                # 9.4 KB  ← main bundle (NO Three.js)
│   ├── massing-study-*.js        # 7.5 KB  ← procedural engine wrapper
│   ├── three-*.js                # 470 KB  ← Three.js (LAZY, on viewport)
│   └── index-*.css               # 18.5 KB
├── models/
│   ├── asset.meta.json           # 6 KB   ← 22-floor underwriting data
│   └── floor-metadata.schema.json
└── img/                          # 240 KB ← portfolio renders
```

**Key insight**: Three.js (470 KB gzipped → 117 KB) only loads when the hero enters the viewport via `IntersectionObserver`. First paint is **9.4 KB**.

---

## The Procedural Engine

`src/three/massing-study.js` generates the tower at runtime using seeded RNG. No two builds are different — same seed = same building.

```javascript
// Floor plate resolution with zone-aware geometry
const widthAt = (floorIndex) => {
  if (floorIndex < PODIUM_FLOORS) return LOT_WIDTH;
  if (floorIndex >= FLOORS - CROWN_FLOORS) return LOT_WIDTH * 0.62;
  return LOT_WIDTH - TOWER_INSET * 2;  // typical tower
};
```

**Features:**
- **22 floors** — Podium (4), Tower (15), Crown (3)
- **Office + Residential variants** — punched windows + balconies for multifamily
- **4 camera views** — Overview, Street, Crown, Plan (smooth spherical interpolation)
- **Floor-by-floor underwriting** — plate, efficiency, glazing, clear height bound to interactive strip
- **Keyboard + touch + mouse** — arrow keys, pinch zoom, Home/End, Enter to select
- **Reduced motion respected** — `prefers-reduced-motion` pauses auto-spin

---

## Lazy-Loading Three.js

The 470 KB chunk loads **only when needed**:

```javascript
// main.js — IntersectionObserver triggers load
const heroSection = document.querySelector('.hero');
const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
  entries.forEach((entry) => {
    if (entry.isIntersecting) {
      io.unobserve(entry.target);
      initWebGL();  // dynamic import('./three/massing-study.js')
    }
  });
}, { rootMargin: '200px 0px', threshold: 0.01 });
io.observe(heroSection);
```

**Result:**
- LCP unaffected by Three.js
- Mobile users who don't scroll to hero never pay the cost
- `prefers-reduced-motion` users never load it

