## Floor Selector + Underwriting Data

The floor strip isn't decorative — it's a **data browser**. Each floor maps to real underwriting metrics:

| Floor | Zone | Plate | Efficiency | Glazing | Clear Height | Use |
|-------|------|-------|------------|---------|--------------|-----|
| 1–4 | Podium | 1,180 sq ft | 78% | 64% | 13'6" | Retail frontage |
| 5–19 | Tower | 1,180 sq ft | 82% | 68% | 13'6" | Grade A office |
| 20–22 | Crown | 940 sq ft | 74% | 71% | 12'6" | Penthouse suite |

Clicking a floor updates the specs panel in real time. The data lives in `public/models/asset.meta.json` — versionable, reviewable, replaceable.

---

## GLTF Upgrade Path (For Buyers)

The procedural engine is the **demo**. Real clients have Revit/Rhino models.

We built a drop-in replacement with **identical API**:

```javascript
// src/three/gltf-loader.js — same { setFocus, setView, destroy }
const { loadGLTFModel } = await import('./three/gltf-loader.js');
study = await loadGLTFModel(canvas, {
  gltfUrl: '/models/building.glb',
  metadataUrl: '/models/building.meta.json',
  onReady: ({ floors }) => { /* same */ },
  onFocus,
});
```

**What buyers need to provide:**
- `building.glb` — Draco-compressed (&lt; 10 MB)
- `building.meta.json` — floor metadata matching GLTF mesh names (`Floor_01`, `Floor_02`...)

Camera views auto-compute from model bounds. No manual config.

---

## Verification Suite (25 Automated Checks)

Every deploy passes 25 Playwright checks:

```bash
# Run locally
BASE=http://localhost:4173 node scripts/verify.mjs
```

| Category | Checks |
|----------|--------|
| **Runtime** | No console errors, WebGL canvas present/sized, hero CTA in viewport |
| **3D** | Floor strip (22), selection updates specs, camera chips respond |
| **Forms** | Rejects invalid, accepts valid, honeypot-ready |
| **A11y** | WCAG AA contrast (4.75:1 light / 6.95:1 dark), keyboard nav, reduced motion |
| **SEO** | JSON-LD (Org, RealEstateAgent, InvestmentFund), sitemap, robots, OG/Twitter |
| **Performance** | No mobile overflow, hero CTA visible, image payload < 600 KB |
| **Security** | CSP meta, service worker, no emoji/gradient headlines |

---

## The License Inquiry Modal

Not a separate page — a modal triggered from Hero + Footer CTAs:

```javascript
// Tracks in dataLayer for GTM
dlPush('license_modal_open', { trigger: 'cta' });
dlPush('license_inquiry_submit', { aum, use_case, firm });
```

Form captures: name, email, firm, AUM range, use case, message. Validates client-side, submits to your endpoint.

